# codezdev-bot environment configuration — copy to .env and fill in real
# values (see CLAUDE.md's "Local testing" section).
#
# This file documents every config knob the Go bot actually reads today.
# It is NOT a port of the Python original's .env.example
# (/Users/z/Desktop/Kiro/.env.example) — that file describes a different,
# larger surface (SePay, PayPal, Binance Pay, AWS IDC, Entra) that this repo
# has deliberately cut. Keys below exist only if the Go source reads them;
# each entry cites the file:line that proves it.
#
# Keys are grouped into four tiers, ordered by how badly things go if you
# get them wrong:
#   TIER 1 — the bot will not start, or will start mis-tenanted.
#   TIER 2 — the bot starts fine, but a whole feature silently disables.
#   TIER 3 — real working defaults; only touch these to tune behavior.
#   TIER 4 — payment-rail knobs; real defaults, but two of them (deposit
#            tolerance, BEP20 confirmation depth) sit directly on money-safety
#            tradeoffs and are worth reading closely before changing.
#
# Where a key is also settable from the in-bot admin wizard, the wizard's
# saved value (settings.json) OVERRIDES whatever is written here. This file
# only sets what settings.json has never touched, or the process-boot values
# (like ADMIN_ID and TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN) that have no wizard equivalent.

# ============================================================================
# TIER 1 — no safe default. Get either of these wrong and the bot does not
# come up as the tenant you expect.
# ============================================================================

# TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN — REQUIRED. No compiled default; an empty value makes
# the bot exit immediately with "TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN not found in .env or
# environment. Refusing to start." (cmd/bot/main.go:105,107).
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=

# ADMIN_ID — the owner / super-admin Telegram chat id. A compiled-in default
# exists (cmd/bot/main.go:77, EnvOr) so the bot boots without this key at
# all. The important part is what NOT to do with it:
#
#   *** DO NOT put ADMIN_ID in .env. Export it AMBIENTLY instead, via
#   *** systemd's `EnvironmentFile=` (or an equivalent process-level env),
#   *** never as a line in this file.
#
# Why: BootGuard (internal/config/config.go:145) treats an ADMIN_ID that is
# UNSET in .env as fine — no mismatch, no complaint (`if v != "" && v !=
# boundValue`). The failure mode runs the other way: ADMIN_ID present in
# .env, absent from the real ambient environment, and different from the
# compiled default — that's when boundValue falls back to the default, the
# two values disagree, and the process log.Fatal's on boot
# (cmd/bot/main.go:98). Putting the key in .env is itself what breaks the
# boot.
#
# The sharper, quieter failure is the reverse case: ambient ADMIN_ID is set
# correctly, and .env ALSO sets ADMIN_ID to something different. Ambient
# always wins during config.Load's merge (internal/config/config.go:36-72):
# the snapshot is seeded from the ambient environment first, then .env only
# fills keys that aren't ALREADY present — so when ambient already has
# ADMIN_ID, the .env line is discarded at merge time and never even enters
# the snapshot BootGuard reads from. BootGuard ends up comparing the ambient
# value against itself, sees no disagreement, and the bot boots perfectly
# fine while silently discarding whatever you wrote in .env. ADMIN_ID is
# BootGuard's only call site today, so this is the one place in the whole
# config surface where writing to .env can either crash the bot or be
# silently thrown away, depending on what the ambient environment has.
# ADMIN_ID=

# ============================================================================
# TIER 2 — a fallback exists, so the bot starts, but the feature it gates
# silently disappears if you leave it unset.
# ============================================================================

# --- API-key product (__apikey__) --------------------------------------
# Unset any of the three KIRO_GO_* keys below and the API-key product simply
# HIDES from the shop instead of selling and failing — this is a deliberate
# invariant (CLAUDE.md "Domain invariants"), not a bug to work around.
# All three are also settable from the admin wizard; a saved settings.json
# value OVERRIDES these (internal/config/settings.go:397-442).

# KIRO_GO_BASE_URL — Kiro-Go proxy base URL (internal/config/settings.go:432,
# wizard override at :428). Unset => API-key product hides.
KIRO_GO_BASE_URL=

# KIRO_GO_ADMIN_KEY — Kiro-Go admin API key (internal/config/settings.go:422,
# wizard override at :418). This is a secret; never log it. Unset => API-key
# product hides.
KIRO_GO_ADMIN_KEY=

# KIRO_GO_ACCOUNT_ID — the Kiro-Go account id credited on every provision
# call (internal/config/settings.go:442, wizard override at :438). Unset =>
# API-key product hides.
KIRO_GO_ACCOUNT_ID=

# KIRO_GO_PUBLIC_URL — the customer-facing dashboard link included with a
# delivered API key (internal/handlers/apikey.go:402). Unset => the key is
# still delivered, just without a dashboard link in the message.
KIRO_GO_PUBLIC_URL=

# --- llmgate direct key minting (bedrock SKU cutover) --------------------
# The bedrock "__apikey__" SKU mints keys DIRECTLY on llmgate via these
# (internal/llmgate; settings.json keys llmgate_base_url / llmgate_username /
# llmgate_password OVERRIDE these — see docs/llmgate-cutover.md). Unset =>
# the bedrock product HIDES, exactly like the KIRO_GO_* rule above. The
# pool keys above remain live for recharges/refunds/stats of pre-cutover
# keys (per-row routing on api_keys.backend) and for the kiro/fixed SKUs.

# LLMGATE_BASE_URL — llmgate CONTROL-PLANE base the bot logs into to mint/
# update/delete keys (internal/config/settings.go LlmgateBaseURL). Default:
# https://api.codezdev-shop.uk (the shop's own Cloudflare-routed host).
LLMGATE_BASE_URL=

# LLMGATE_USERNAME / LLMGATE_PASSWORD — the llmgate account credentials
# (internal/config/settings.go LlmgateUsername/LlmgatePassword). The password
# is a secret; never log it. The client caches the ~30-day login token and
# re-logins on expiry by itself.
LLMGATE_USERNAME=
LLMGATE_PASSWORD=

# LLMGATE_API_BASE — the PUBLIC completions endpoint shown to CUSTOMERS in
# the delivery message's "recommended" Base URL line (internal/config
# LlmgateAPIBase). Distinct from LLMGATE_BASE_URL so either host can move
# independently; today both are https://api.codezdev-shop.uk.
LLMGATE_API_BASE=

# LLMGATE_PUBLIC_URL — the host of the SHOP'S WEB PAGES shown in the
# delivery message's dashboard/docs/models links (internal/config
# LlmgatePublicURL). Needs its own knob because the web pages (shop-web)
# can live on a different host than the API. Default falls back to
# KIRO_GO_PUBLIC_URL, then the Kiro-Go base, then the LLMGATE_API_BASE
# value.
LLMGATE_PUBLIC_URL=

# --- On-chain payment addresses -----------------------------------------
# Both are wizard-writable; a saved settings.json address OVERRIDES these
# (internal/config/settings.go:397-411).

# BEP20_ADDRESS — the seller's USDT-BEP20 (BNB Smart Chain) receiving address
# (internal/config/settings.go:401). Unset => the BEP20 payment rail hides
# from checkout.
BEP20_ADDRESS=

# TRON_ADDRESS — the seller's USDT-TRC20 (TRON) receiving address
# (internal/config/settings.go:411). Unset => the TRON payment rail hides
# from checkout.
TRON_ADDRESS=

# --- Misc fallbacks -------------------------------------------------------

# TRON_API_KEY — TronGrid API key (internal/config/config.go:111). Works
# unset, but TronGrid rate-limits unauthenticated/free-tier callers harder,
# which shows up as slower or failed deposit confirmation polling under load.
TRON_API_KEY=

# SUPPORT_HANDLE — pins the bot's support @handle. Unset => the bot instead
# resolves the owner's LIVE @username by id at boot (cmd/bot/main.go:117),
# which keeps working across a username rename; setting this disables that
# auto-resolve, so a rename with this set will leave customers messaging a
# stale handle.
SUPPORT_HANDLE=

# USD_TO_VND — the VND-per-USD rate the whole shop prices against. Every
# customer-facing amount and every on-chain deposit is quoted through it, so
# a wrong value here misprices the entire catalogue at once.
#
# The admin wizard writes this into settings.json, and SETTINGS.JSON WINS
# over this file — if the displayed rate disagrees with what you set here,
# that is why; change it in the bot rather than here.
#
# Accepted range is 1000..200000, whole numbers only. That bound is enforced
# in two places now: the wizard refuses anything outside it, and the reader
# refuses it too, so a hand-edited settings.json cannot smuggle in a rate the
# wizard would have rejected. A rejected value is IGNORED and logged by name,
# and the effective rate falls back to this file and then to the compiled
# default — you will see a line naming the key and the bad value, so nothing
# fails silently.
#
# Note this file's value is NOT range-checked the way settings.json is: it is
# parsed and used if it looks like a positive number. Reaching this file
# needs server access rather than the admin UI, which is the reason for the
# difference, not an oversight.
#
# Kept deliberately during the VND->USDT ledger migration: the ledger is
# still denominated in VND, and this rate is what the one-shot conversion is
# frozen against. Do not remove it until that migration has run and the
# application has been switched over.
USD_TO_VND=

# ============================================================================
# TIER 3 — real working defaults. Everything below is optional tuning; the
# bot behaves sanely if you leave all of it commented out.
# ============================================================================
#
# Five of the loop-interval keys below — EXPIRY_SWEEP_INTERVAL,
# RECONCILE_STUCK_INTERVAL_S, STOCK_SWEEP_INTERVAL_S, USDT_CONFIRM_POLL_S
# and USDT_WATCH_INTERVAL_S — are read through b.envDuration, which carries a
# MINIMUM-INTERVAL FLOOR: a value set below the floor is silently raised to
# the floor, and the raise is LOGGED at startup. AUDIT_RETENTION_DAYS has its
# own, separate floor (noted at its own entry below). Every other key in
# this tier (USDT_PENDING_GRACE_S, USDT_VERIFY_GRACE_S, USDT_CONFIRM_WAIT_S,
# USDT_MAX_POLLS, the PRODUCT_CLICK_* trio, MIN/MAX_DEPOSIT_USDT) is read
# through b.envInt/envFloat with NO floor — set one of those to an
# unreasonably small value and it takes effect exactly as given, no clamp,
# no log line.

# AUDIT_RETENTION_DAYS — how many days of audit-log rows the janitor keeps
# before pruning (internal/handlers/auditprune.go:78,41). Default: 180. A
# value below the compiled floor (auditprune.go:56) is raised to the floor
# and logged.
AUDIT_RETENTION_DAYS=180

# MIN_DEPOSIT_USDT / MAX_DEPOSIT_USDT — the accepted deposit amount range in
# USDT (internal/handlers/deposit.go:60-61). Defaults: 1 / 100000.
MIN_DEPOSIT_USDT=1
MAX_DEPOSIT_USDT=100000

# PRODUCT_CLICK_LIMIT / PRODUCT_CLICK_WINDOW_S / PRODUCT_CLICK_COOLDOWN_S —
# per-chat rate limiting on product-list clicks: at most LIMIT clicks per
# WINDOW_S seconds, then a COOLDOWN_S-second lockout
# (internal/handlers/dispatch.go:297-299). Defaults: 10 clicks / 60s window /
# 60s cooldown.
PRODUCT_CLICK_LIMIT=10
PRODUCT_CLICK_WINDOW_S=60
PRODUCT_CLICK_COOLDOWN_S=60

# EXPIRY_SWEEP_INTERVAL — how often the periodic janitor sweeps expired order
# reservations back to active stock (internal/handlers/dispatch.go:352).
# Default: 120s. Carries a minimum-interval floor — see note above.
EXPIRY_SWEEP_INTERVAL=120s

# RECONCILE_STUCK_INTERVAL_S — how often the report-only stuck-order
# reconcile pass runs; it only logs an owner alert for paid-but-undelivered
# orders, never delivers or refunds on its own
# (internal/handlers/dispatch.go:357). Default: 600s.
RECONCILE_STUCK_INTERVAL_S=600

# STOCK_SWEEP_INTERVAL_S — how often the folder-stock janitor reclaims
# abandoned reservations (internal/handlers/dispatch.go:362). Default: 300s.
# This sweep takes the same per-product mutex the live buy path uses, so too
# tight a loop contends against real customer purchases — the sharpest edge
# of this port's env-driven loop intervals.
STOCK_SWEEP_INTERVAL_S=300

# USDT_PENDING_GRACE_S — how long a dead (no longer active) deposit "band"
# still counts toward matching an incoming transfer, before eviction
# (internal/handlers/dispatch.go:366; internal/pay/bands/registry.go).
# Default: 7200s (2h).
USDT_PENDING_GRACE_S=7200

# USDT_VERIFY_GRACE_S — extra grace window while verifying a deposit match
# (internal/handlers/dispatch.go:367). Default: 120s.
USDT_VERIFY_GRACE_S=120

# USDT_CONFIRM_WAIT_S — how long the bot waits for on-chain confirmation
# before giving up on a single confirm attempt
# (internal/handlers/dispatch.go:368). Default: 300s.
USDT_CONFIRM_WAIT_S=300

# USDT_CONFIRM_POLL_S — polling interval while waiting for confirmation
# (internal/handlers/dispatch.go:369). Default: 20s. Carries a minimum floor.
USDT_CONFIRM_POLL_S=20

# USDT_MAX_POLLS — hard cap on total confirm-polls, globally, across all
# chats at once (internal/handlers/dispatch.go:370). Default: 200.
USDT_MAX_POLLS=200

# USDT_WATCH_INTERVAL_S — how often the hands-free deposit watcher reads the
# TRON seller address for incoming transfers (internal/handlers/usdtwatch.go).
# Default: 20s. Carries a minimum floor.
#
# This is roughly how long a customer waits between their transfer confirming
# on-chain and their balance moving, so shorter feels better — but each tick
# with any deposit open is one TronGrid call, and unlike the confirm poll this
# loop runs for the whole life of every open deposit rather than for one
# customer's few-minute wait. Getting the shop's own address rate-limited
# would break hash verification for every rail at once, so raise this rather
# than lower it if TronGrid starts complaining. A tick with NO deposit open
# makes no call at all.
USDT_WATCH_INTERVAL_S=20

# --- Account-provisioning subprocess knobs --------------------------------
# NOT in the original task list for this file — found while verifying the
# config surface. These back the kiro-*-login.py / .mjs helper scripts that
# internal/provision and internal/handlers/otp.go run as subprocesses
# (CLAUDE.md "Account provisioning"). All three have working defaults.

# KIRO_LOGIN_PYTHON — the Python interpreter used to run the browser-login
# subprocess scripts (internal/config/config.go:121). Default: "python3".
KIRO_LOGIN_PYTHON=python3

# KIRO_NODE — the Node binary used to run the .mjs helper scripts
# (internal/handlers/otp.go:646). Default: "node". The override exists
# because a Go deployment host may not have node on the service PATH.
KIRO_NODE=node

# KIRO_SCRIPT_DIR — directory holding the bot's sibling helper scripts
# (fetch_login_code.mjs and friends) (internal/handlers/otp.go:680). Default:
# the running executable's own directory.
KIRO_SCRIPT_DIR=

# KIRO_ARCHIVE_DIR — where archived provisioned-key JSON records land
# (internal/handlers/adminstock.go:1933). Default: a gitignored directory
# next to the binary.
KIRO_ARCHIVE_DIR=

# ============================================================================
# TIER 4 — payment-rail knobs. These were dead in production until the fix
# in commits b8be4fc/154e238 (~an hour before this file was written); every
# key below now genuinely reaches the code that reads it.
# ============================================================================

# DEPOSIT_MATCH_TOL_UNITS — how far a received USDT deposit amount may differ
# from the quoted amount and still be accepted as a match on the deposit-credit
# path (internal/pay/bands/credit.go). Default: 50.
#
# RENAMED from DEPOSIT_MATCH_TOL_CENTS, which is no longer read at all: the
# value is in AMOUNT UNITS at the rail's *_AMOUNT_DECIMALS, and those are now 5
# (1e-5 USDT), so 50 = 0.00050 USDT. Setting it in cents would be off by a
# factor of a thousand. Whatever you set is silently CAPPED at the rail's own
# *_MATCH_TOL, because a deposit tolerance wider than half the band spacing
# would let one payment match two live orders' amounts.
DEPOSIT_MATCH_TOL_UNITS=50

# BEP20_MIN_CONF — reorg safety: how many BSC blocks a transfer must be
# buried under before the sale is considered settled
# (internal/pay/bep20/bep20.go:95, resolved through config at
# internal/handlers/dispatch.go:393). Default: 12.
#
# Lowering this accepts more chain-reversal risk: a transfer that looked
# confirmed can still get reorg'd out, which would mean stock or an API key
# was already delivered against a deposit that later stops existing. Don't
# lower it without understanding that tradeoff.
BEP20_MIN_CONF=12

# BEP20_WATCH_LOOKBACK_BLOCKS — the hands-free BEP20 watcher's fetch window,
# in blocks: it reads [head-lookback, head] every tick. Default: 5000.
# (internal/handlers/dispatch.go, usdtwatch.go's tickBep20.) A FIXED trailing
# window (not a timestamp-derived offset) so it can't slide past a promptly-paid
# transfer under variable block times. Two constraints: it must cover the pending
# grace at the fastest plausible block time (5000 ~ covers 2h at 1.5s blocks),
# AND stay under the BSC node's eth_getLogs range cap. If a node caps below your
# setting the watcher logs "fetch failed" every tick and no BEP20 deposit credits
# hands-free — lower this to fit.
BEP20_WATCH_LOOKBACK_BLOCKS=5000

# USDT_BAND_EVICT_S — pressure-only soft-eviction window for a dead deposit
# band (internal/pay/bands/registry.go:39). Default: 1800s (30m).
USDT_BAND_EVICT_S=1800

# BEP20_AMOUNT_DECIMALS / BEP20_MATCH_TOL / BEP20_OFFSET_STEP — BEP20 unique-
# amount matching: decimal precision used, tolerance window, and the offset
# step used to make each pending order's quoted amount unique
# (internal/pay/bep20/bep20.go). Defaults: 5 / 50 / 101.
#
# THESE THREE ARE A SET. Every quoted amount is the price plus a jitter of
# 0.01000-0.01999 USDT, and the slots inside that window must stay at least
# 2*MATCH_TOL+1 units apart or one payment could settle two orders. The shipped
# 5 / 50 / 101 sits exactly on the 2*50+1 boundary and fits ten slots per price.
#
# What REFUSES TO BOOT: AMOUNT_DECIMALS outside [2,9]; an OFFSET_STEP wider than
# the window (1000 units at 5 decimals), which leaves room for only one order
# per price; a MATCH_TOL wider than the window, same reason from the other side.
#
# What only WARNS in the log: an OFFSET_STEP below 2*MATCH_TOL+1. Amounts stay
# disjoint either way — the picker re-checks the gap per slot — but capacity
# collapses, so customers start seeing "too many pending payments" for no
# visible reason. Raise MATCH_TOL without raising OFFSET_STEP and that is what
# you get; the boot log says so explicitly.
#
# UPGRADE NOTE: the previous 2 / 10 / 21 was superseded — a .env still carrying
# those values fails validation and the bot refuses to start. Delete the lines
# to take the defaults.
BEP20_AMOUNT_DECIMALS=5
BEP20_MATCH_TOL=50
BEP20_OFFSET_STEP=101

# TRON_AMOUNT_DECIMALS / TRON_MATCH_TOL / TRON_OFFSET_STEP / TRON_PAGE_LIMIT
# / TRON_API_BASE — the TRON-rail equivalents of the BEP20 matching knobs
# above (same set-of-three rule), plus the TronGrid page size and API base URL
# (internal/pay/tron/tron.go). Defaults: 5 / 50 / 101 / 200 /
# https://api.trongrid.io.
TRON_AMOUNT_DECIMALS=5
TRON_MATCH_TOL=50
TRON_OFFSET_STEP=101
TRON_PAGE_LIMIT=200
TRON_API_BASE=https://api.trongrid.io

# BEP20_QR_URL / BEP20_QR_PATH / TRON_QR_URL / TRON_QR_PATH — hosted-image
# URL or local file path for the deposit-screen QR code of the seller's
# address, one pair per rail (internal/pay/bep20/bep20.go:167,173;
# internal/pay/tron/tron.go:177,183). Unset => no QR image is sent, only the
# text address.
#
# *** LIVE CAVEAT: as of this writing these four are read with raw
# *** os.Getenv (internal/pay/bep20/bep20.go:167,173;
# *** internal/pay/tron/tron.go:177,183) instead of through the Config
# *** snapshot — and config.Load parses .env into its own in-memory map
# *** rather than exporting it into the process environment
# *** (internal/config/config.go:36-72). So a value set ONLY in this .env
# *** file is invisible to these four keys today; the same value set in the
# *** AMBIENT environment (systemd EnvironmentFile or equivalent) works
# *** right now. The delivery path itself (QRURL/QRPath -> sendOnchainQR ->
# *** SendPhoto, internal/handlers/usdt.go:499-539) is fully wired — it is
# *** only these four reads that skip .env. A fix to route them through
# *** Config is in flight; once it lands, setting these here will work too.
BEP20_QR_URL=
BEP20_QR_PATH=
TRON_QR_URL=
TRON_QR_PATH=
